          "segment_id": "seg-994112f39f68401f786b3d1d",
          "segment_index": 12,
          "source_segment_id": "seg-994112f39f68401f786b3d1d",
          "source_text_sha256": "b421196a28ab52152e13e6d37e28849cf90c5f91e867f64b003e80184f3c87ac",
          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Summary: Observation of the movement of three bright points in the sky: observation of the Chinese satellite triplet Yaogan-31 A, B, and C.",
          "translation_text_sha256": "5890ad2ce84355421e31731a519ec9c664fa612ad893b6becd31d76c28be1270"
        },
        {
          "end_ms": null,
          "error": null,
          "field": "description",
          "page_id": "page-1bd61a9cde7fef7c658d4073",
          "qa_findings": [],
          "review_status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "segment_id": "seg-bd79354f25afcb06325aae17",
          "segment_index": 13,
          "source_segment_id": "seg-bd79354f25afcb06325aae17",
          "source_text_sha256": "066b9385c0b235cdaecd16701332f3308e8e7f66a6c674c08e378a77437f7227",
          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On December 18, 2020, as night fell, the witness (with his daughter) had his attention drawn to a very bright constellation composed of 3 points, forming a quasi-equilateral triangle. The phenomenon began to change in brightness and seemed to be moving. After a few seconds, less than a minute, each point eventually disappeared almost simultaneously. It looked like \"3 ISS\" forming a triangle. The consistency of this case is average, with only one witness report, though it is well-detailed, there is no photo or video of the PAN. The investigation revealed that the witnesses observed a trio of Chinese satellites, in a temporary alignment that made them visible to the naked eye; that is, the sun reflected off each satellite towards the witness. This conclusion is based on the following elements: - Number: three satellites moving in unison. This is typical of such satellites. - The appearance is entirely consistent with that of satellites (brightness, color, point-like appearance, straight-line motion), which the witness also noted independently. - The presence in the sky at the time of the observation of these satellites is confirmed (see data provided by the Operational Space Surveillance Center of CNES). - The elevations given by the witness correspond to the trajectory of the triplet within 1.5 minutes. - The estimated duration, of a few seconds, less than a minute, is consistent with the visibility duration of these flashes; it is also consistent with cases already studied by GEIPAN (for example, 30 to 50 seconds for the PETIT-QUEVILLY (LE) (76) 16.04.2014 case and 8 seconds for SOUSTONS (40) 01.12.2019). - The direction of observation was correctly estimated, as was the angular separation between each of the triplet components (5°). Classification as \"A\", certain observation of a trio of Chinese Yaogan-31 satellites A, B, and C. The witness observes the reflection of the sun on these 3 satellites.",
          "translation_text_sha256": "b895ee560ba696540b802a09fd5b118cf81ed0fd1240009837d94a74b17571e5"
        }
      ],
